     1,
     "<div>Hello everyone, <br></div><div><br></div><div>I have a RI-CLPM (RICLPM5 from <a href=\"https://jeroendmulder.github.io/RI-CLPM/lavaan.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://jeroendmulder.github.io/RI-CLPM/lavaan.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792414739766000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0iR_WmKxJYcgb2YPwwo3Q1\">Moulder &amp; Hamaker</a>) with four measurement occasions and constraints over time. I have to compute 2*9 models where x-parameters always have the same scale, but the scales of the y-parameters are different from x-parameters and differ from the first 9 models to the second 9 models. <br></div><div>Hence, I am interested in having not only constrained cross-lagged Estimates, but them also standardized. <br></div><div><br></div><div>The &quot;Estimates&quot; are nicely equivalent, but the Std.all-values differ having &quot;standardized=T&quot; in the summary-function, e.g.:</div><div><br></div><div>\r\n\r\n<span aria-label=\"Console Output\" role=\"document\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;outline:none;border:medium;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.2;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial\"><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\"><span style=\"outline:none;border:medium;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap\"><font size=\"2\">Regressions:\r\n                   Estimate  Std.Err  z-value  P(&gt;|z|)   Std.lv  Std.all\r\n  wx2 ~                                                                 \r\n    wx1        (a)    0.621    0.064    9.716    0.000    0.485    0.485\r\n    wy1        (b)   -0.112    0.103   -1.082    0.279   -0.068   -0.068\r\n  wy2 ~                         