eak-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap\"><font size=\"2\">    0.047    1.086    0.277    0.097    </font></span></span></span><span aria-label=\"Console Output\" role=\"document\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;outline:none;border:medium;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.2;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial;color:rgb(255,0,0)\"><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\"><span style=\"outline:none;border:medium;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap\"><font size=\"2\"><b>0.097</b></font></span></span></span><span aria-label=\"Console Output\" role=\"document\" style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;,monospace;outline:none;border:medium;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.2;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);text-decoration-style:initial;text-decoration-color:initial\"><span role=\"document\" style=\"outline:none\"><span style=\"outline:none;border:medium;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap\"><font size=\"2\">\r\n    wy3        (d)    0.184    0.069    2.671    0.008    0.184    0.184</font></span></span></span>\r\n\r\n</div><div><br></div><div>I thought about standardizing all parameters before they enter the model (e.g., with &quot;std.ov=T&quot;) and reporting the (constrained) &quot;Estimates&quot; and still call them &quot;Beta&quot; (for the standardized regression coefficient), but I don&#39;t know if this is valid / truly equivalent. </div><div><br></div><div>Can you help me finding the true standardized and constrained estimates?</div><div><br></div><div>PS:</div><div>The Model Syntax (from Moulder&amp;Hamaker): <br></div><div><span style=\"font-family:Courier New\"><font size=\"2\">RICLPM5 &lt;- &#39;<br>  # Create between components (random intercepts)<br>  RIx =~ 1*x1 + 1*x2 + 1*x3 + 1*x4 <br>  RIy =~ 1*y1 + 1*y2 + 1*y3 + 1*y4 <br>    # Create within-person centered variables<br>  wx1 =~ 1*x1<br>  wx2 =~ 1*x2<br>  wx3 =~ 1*x3 <br>  wx4 =~ 1*x4<br>  wy1 =~ 1*y1<br>  wy2 =~ 1*y2<br>  wy3 =~ 1*y3<br>  wy4 =~ 1*y4<br> <br>  # Estimate lagged effects between within-person centered variables <br>  # (constrained)<br>  wx2 ~ a*wx1 + b*wy1 <br>  wy2 ~ c*wx1 + d*wy1<br>  wx3 ~ a*wx2 + b*wy2<br>  wy3 ~ c*wx2 + d*wy2<br>  wx4 ~ a*wx3 + b*wy3<br>  wy4 ~ c*wx3 + d*wy3<br><br>  # Estimate covariances between residuals of within-person centered variables <br>  # (i.e., innovations, constrained)<br>  wx2 ~~ cov*wy2<br>  wx3 ~~ cov*wy3<br>  wx4 ~~ cov*wy4 <br><br>  # Estimate covariance between within-person centered variables at first wave<br>  wx1 ~~ wy1 # Covariance<br>  <br>  # Estimate variance and covariance of random intercepts<br>  RIx ~~ RIx<br>  RIy ~~ RIy<br>  RIx ~~ RIy<br>  <br>  # Estimate (residual) variance of within-person centered variables <br>  # (constrained)<br>  wx1 ~~ wx1 # Variance<br>  wy1 ~~ wy1 <br>  wx2 ~~ vx*wx2 # Residual variance<br>  wy2 ~~ vy*wy2 <br>  wx3 ~~ vx*wx3 <br>  wy3 ~~ vy*wy3 <br>  wx4 ~~ vx*wx4 <br>  wy4 ~~ vy*wy4 <br><br>  # Constrain grand means over time<br>  x1 + x2 + x3 + x4  ~ mx*1<br>  y1 + y2 + y3 + y4  ~ my*1&#39;</font></span></div></blockquote></div>"
